  "sentence": "Model (`node model.mjs`, every assumption is a flag): starting from today's 16%, at the fade the data implies (Intents' growth halving about every 1.0 quarters, see below) the buyback reaches half of net issuance not within 10 years; with a slower fade, halving every 2 quarters (the default flag), in 2027-Q4 (4 quarters); with no further growth it stays at 16%; if the measured 1.80× per 90 days never fades, in 2027-Q2 (2 quarters). A scenario, not a forecast. The measured quarter-on-quarter growth went 6.3× → 5.7× → 2.3× → 0.7× → 1.1× → 1.8×; fading from the oldest quarter to the latest four implies a half-life of about 1.0 quarters, so the 2-quarter default is on the generous side. The bought-back NEAR sits in a multisig (held, not burned); `--resold` models some of it returning to market. If HSP-029 (max issuance 2.5% → 1.6% over 24 months; House of Stake vote 99.97% for, timelock until 2026-11-16; no start date set) began its ramp now: at the implied fade, in 2028-Q4 (8 quarters); at the 2-quarter default, in 2027-Q3 (3 quarters)."
 },
